## Context

Two test gaps identified after reviewing the archive and log commands:

1. `erg archive` in ID mode applies the same blocker-guard as default mode
   (SKIPPED when a closed ticket is still referenced by an open Blocked-by),
   but no test covered the ID-mode path.

2. `cmdLog` in `log.go` calls `appendLogLine` even when the ticket file has no
   `--- body ---` separator, silently corrupting the file structure.

## Actions

- Add ID-mode blocker-guard test to `tests/test_archive.sh`
- Fix `cmdLog` in `tickets/tools/go/log.go` to refuse writes when the separator
  is missing
- Add missing-separator test to `tests/test_log.sh`

## Exit criteria

- `make test-archive` passes with new ID-mode blocker tests green
- `make test-log` passes with new missing-separator test green
- `erg log` exits non-zero with a "body" error message when the ticket has no
  `--- body ---` separator
